  "glossaryRoiTerm": "ROI (Return on Investment)",
  "glossaryRoiDef": "Measures how much you recover for every dollar invested in a crop. It is calculated as (Income − Expenses) ÷ Expenses. A negative ROI means the crop spends more than it recovers: for example, an ROI of −70% means that for every $100 invested only $30 come back.",
